 You need a professional report to submit as supporting documentation for a military waiver request. [...] If you are pursuing a career in the U.S. military or law enforcement, navigating the medical clearance process at the Military Entrance Processing Station (MEPS) can be challenging. A history of an ADHD diagnosis, childhood learning differences, or past mental health treatment often triggers a temporary disqualification. However, an official medical disqualification is not the end of your journey—it simply means you need a formal waiver review supported by a rigorous, independent psychological [...] Evaluations may be completed in person or virtually for applicants located in participating PSYPACT states. View the PSYPACT map.

## Before Your Appointment

You will be asked to:

 Complete a detailed history questionnaire;
 Submit the records requested for review, such as mental health treatment or medication records; and
 Provide any documentation or specific questions supplied by your recruiter or MEPS.
